{"availability":"available","full":"vishalyl/diabetic-retinopathy-detection","name":"diabetic-retinopathy-detection","description":"Measuring patient-level data leakage in diabetic retinopathy grading, a validated both-eyes ensembling method, two quantum ML experiments, and a Gradio screening demo -- all with pre-registered acceptance tests.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-13T12:19:31Z","updated":"2026-09-21T07:15:16Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/vishal1829/fundus-console","topics":["computer-vision","data-leakage","deep-learning","diabetic-retinopathy","gradio","healthcare-ai","medical-imaging","pytorch","quantum-machine-learning","reproducible-research"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/vishal1829/fundus-console","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.664Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.664Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.664Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.664Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A diabetic retinopathy grading study built around one methodological question: what happens to your reported accuracy when you split retinal images by image instead of by patient?","The answer, measured directly on 17,563 patients: a 0.8545 inter-eye quadratic-weighted kappa (QWK), and a lookup table that guesses a patient's grade from only their other eye's label — no image data at all — scores QWK 0.838. That's how much signal leaks across a patient's two eyes into a naive train/test split, and it's the reason this project evaluates everything on a patient-level split (P2), never the image-level split (P1) most tutorials use.","Everything below — the leakage measurement, the final screening model, the both-eyes ensembling method, and two honestly-negative quantum machine learning experiments — was measured with pre-registered acceptance tests, patient-level bootstrap confidence intervals, and one rule enforced throughout: no claim ships without a check that could have failed it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vishalyl/diabetic-retinopathy-detection/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"884b2e2ee3ca76ebd1d9d03dcf6b5c82505548c08d957f0b70d5637b1ed1428b","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.776Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.776Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A diabetic retinopathy grading study built around one methodological question: what happens to your reported accuracy when you split retinal images by image instead of by patient?","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vishalyl/diabetic-retinopathy-detection/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"884b2e2ee3ca76ebd1d9d03dcf6b5c82505548c08d957f0b70d5637b1ed1428b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vishalyl/diabetic-retinopathy-detection/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.777Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-21T07:15:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vishalyl/diabetic-retinopathy-detection/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:33:46.779Z","hash":"884b2e2ee3ca76ebd1d9d03dcf6b5c82505548c08d957f0b70d5637b1ed1428b","originalBytes":12023,"storedBytes":12023,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["app","model","qwk","results","test","both","eyes","one","checkpoint","experiments","release","acceptance","data","own","quantum","same","src","two","patient","project","see","split","deployed","does","every","features","qml","tests","what","aptos","classical","head","patient-level","raw","run","their","train","arxiv","best","card.md","claim","configs","datasets","diabetic","eyepacs","grade","image","leakage","live","master","nbsp","number","plan.md","pre-registered","recall","retinopathy","above","actually","al.","any","before","below","bootstrap","built","card","classifier","cnn","confidence","config","console","converge